-- title:
--   Index of Γ∩ s⁻¹Γ s equals degeneracy degree
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a_2,b_2$, a non-zero squarefree natural number $N$ and primes $q,q'$ with $q\nmid N$, $q'\nmid N$, $q'\neq q$ and $q,q'\ge 5$, and assume `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a₂ b₂ q`: $a_2<0$, $b_2<0$, and for each finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ the completion $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q$ lies in $v$. Let $\Lambda_2$ be a maximal order (an order maximal among orders) and $R_2\le\Lambda_2$ an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. an intersection of two maximal orders whose relative index in the first is $N$. Let $n_2$ be a finite-adelic unit in `primeHeckeSet R₂ q'` (it lies in the finite adelic box of $R_2$, as does $q'\cdot n_2^{-1}$, while $n_2^{-1}$ and $q'^{-1}n_2$ do not), and assume the meet order $R_2\cap n_2R_2n_2^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nq'$. Let $v_1$ be a place containing $q'$, let $\ell$ be a prime distinct from $q$ and $q'$, and let $s$ be a global unit and $sf$ a finite-adelic unit such that $sf$ has component $s\otimes 1$ at every place not containing $q'$ and component $1$ at places containing $q'$, the product of the diagonal idele of the scalar $\ell$ with $sf^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₂ (meetOrder R₂ n₂) ℓ` when $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₂ n₂) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s)=\ell$. Finally let $\Gamma$ be the subgroup of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]^\times$ consisting of those $x$ whose image in $(\mathrm{Loc}\,a_2\,b_2\,w)^\times$ lies in the subgroup generated by the local box units of $R_2$ at $w$ for every place $w\neq v_1$, and for which $v_{q'}(\mathrm{nrd}\,x)$ is even. Then the relative index of $\Gamma\cap s^{-1}\Gamma s$ in $\Gamma$ equals `HeckeTower.arrowDegree N (ℓ, 1)`, that is $\ell$ if $\ell\mid N$ and $\ell+1$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the local degree computation for a degeneracy map in the Hecke tower: the index of $\Gamma\cap s^{-1}\Gamma s$ in $\Gamma$ for an element $s$ of reduced norm $\ell$ reproduces the bidegree $\ell+1$ (or $\ell$ at levels dividing $N$) of the $\ell$-Hecke correspondence. It is the companion, for the arrow tag $1$, of the statement for $\Gamma\cap s\Gamma s^{-1}$, and is used in the construction of the quotient presentation of the class set and in the realisation statements for the Čerednik–Drinfeld descent intertwining.
